(7144160, 1094295, 25024, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nadine_Vb:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kathy:</b></div><hr/><i> Sorry, but I just didn''t "get" this one (regardless of the challenge theme.) I''d love to know what it is. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Didn''t see the jiggsaw puzzle? pieces <i>matching</i> into each other.<br/>Great macro, nice monochrome and far underrated! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sorry Kathy, but you weren''t alone! It would appear to have been far too subtle for most people here but glad you understood and appreciated it Nadine, thank you both for commenting.<br/> <br/>The title, by the way, was a play on words, the piece being the completion of an elephants tusk in the jigsaw but also signifying task complete as in last piece of the jigsaw - ah well!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-12-18 07:00:10.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Nadine_Vb: Originally posted by Kathy: Sorry, but I just didn''t "get" this one (regardless of the challenge theme.) I''d love to know what it is.   Didn''t see the jiggsaw puzzle? pieces matching into each other.Great macro, nice monochrome and far underrated!   Sorry Kathy, but you weren''t alone! It would appear to have been far too subtle for most people here but glad you understood and appreciated it Nadine, thank you both for commenting. The title, by the way, was a play on words, the piece being the completion of an elephants tusk in the jigsaw but also signifying task complete as in last piece of the jigsaw - ah well!', '2013-12-18 06:55:58.000000', '2013-12-18 07:00:10.000000', 0),
